\n      \"kind\": \"parameter\",\n      \"role\": \"admissibility\",\n      \"statement\": \"The parameter is m=4.\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"source_clause_id\": \"c-question\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"constraint_id\": \"20.50-generated-by-four-involutions\",\n      \"kind\": \"object_class\",\n      \"role\": \"admissibility\",\n      \"statement\": \"G_4 is generated by four involutions; each of the four specified generators has order exactly 2.\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"source_clause_id\": \"c-definition\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"constraint_id\": \"20.50-all-involutions-relation\",\n      \"kind\": \"relation\",\n      \"role\": \"admissibility\",\n      \"statement\": \"For every pair x,y that are involutions anywhere in G_4, not merely for pairs of the four chosen generators, (xy)^4=1.\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"source_clause_id\": \"c-definition\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"constraint_id\": \"20.50-largest-universal-object\",\n      \"kind\": \"definition\",\n      \"role\": \"admissibility\",\n      \"statement\": \"The target is the largest/universal group in this class, so a quotient or one finite example is not automatically G_4.\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"source_clause_id\": \"c-definition\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"constraint_id\": \"20.50-determine-order\",\n      \"kind\": \"conclusion\",\n      \"role\": \"target_conclusion\",\n      \"statement\": \"Determine |G_4| exactly, including proving finiteness if a finite integer is claimed.\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"source_clause_id\": \"c-question\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"excluded_scopes\": [\n    \"The known m=3 case\",\n    \"Groups imposing (xy)^4=1 only on pairs of chosen generators\",\n    \"A finite quotient not proved equal to the universal G_4\"\n  ],\n  \"success_criteria\": {\n    \"proof\": \"Determine |G_4| exactly and prove that the computed/presented object has the required universal property.\",\n    \"counterexample\": \"If the presupposed finite order fails, prove the universal object infinite or prove that no largest object exists under the source definition.\",\n    \"partial_progress\": [\n      \"A certified finite quotient/lower bound together with a clear statement that it is not yet the universal group.\",\n      \"A proved structural or nilpotency reduction applying to every four-generated group in the class.\"\n    ],\n    \"certificate\": \"A checkable confluent presentation, p-quotient/collection certificate plus a universality proof, or a rigorous infinitude certificate.\"\n  },\n  \"selection_status\": \"approved\",\n  \"state\": \"reconnaissance\",\n  \"scope_answered\": false,\n  \"active_direction\": \"proof\",\n  \"truth_likelihood\": {\n    \"estimate\": 0.62,\n    \"rationale\": \"Here 'truth' means that the intended universal object is finite and has a determinable order; the m=3 context favors finiteness but does not settle m=4.\",\n    \"updated_utc\": \"2026-08-16T11:13:07Z\"\n  },\n  \"priority\": {\n    \"importance\": 4,\n    \"probability_of_substantial_progress\": 0.3,\n    \"verifiability\": 4,\n    \"expected_active_hours\": 3.0,\n    \"rationale\": \"The exact target is important and certificate-shaped, but universal-property verification is substantially harder than finding a quotient.\"\n  },\n  \"direction_sessions\": {\n    \"proof\": {\n      \"session_id\": null,\n      \"state\": \"not_started\",\n      \"parent_session_id\": null,\n      \"fresh_session_reason\": \"First protocol-v2 activation as the clear reserve replacing the convention-blocked 21.90 slot.\"\n    },\n    \"counterexample\": {\n      \"session_id\": null,\n      \"state\": \"not_started\",\n      \"parent_session_id\": null,\n      \"fresh_session_reason\": null\n    }\n  },\n  \"current_strategy\": \"derive universal structural constraints before any bounded quotient computation\",\n  \"strategy_history\": [],\n  \"latest_outcome\": \"selected as clear reserve pending scope audit\",\n  \"open_questions\": [],\n  \"revision_history\": [\n    {\n      \"revision\": 1,\n      \"changed_utc\": \"2026-08-16T11:13:07Z\",\n      \"reason\": \"Initial protocol-v2 activation as replacement for a definition-blocked slot.\",\n      \"supersedes\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"blind_run\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"open_web\": false,\n    \"solution_bearing_history_allowed\": false,\n    \"claim_of_clean_pretraining\": false\n  },\n  \"updated_utc\": \"2026-08-16T11:48:00Z\"\n}\n---\ntitle: \"Clean-context brief: 20.50 four-involution universal group\"\nauthor: operator\ntags: [agent/lead, user/operator, domain/group-theory, topic/kourovka, topic/presentations, project/kourovka, status/draft]\n---\n\n# Active statement\n\nDetermine the order of the largest group (G_4) generated by four involutions and\nsatisfying ((xy)^4=1) for every pair of involutions (x,y\\in G_4).\n\n# Scope trap\n\nThe relation ranges over all involutions in the group, not only over pairs of the\nfour chosen generators. A finite quotient or a group satisfying generator-pair\nrelations is not automatically the universal (G_4).\n\n# Direction and first strategy\n\nThe planning estimate is 0.62 that the intended universal object is finite, so this\nrun starts in the proof/determination direction. First derive structural\nconsequences that apply to every group in the class and specify what would prove\nuniversality. Use bounded quotient computation only after the target object and\ncertificate are explicit.\n\n# Clean-context boundary\n\nUse the source PDF, canonical scope, this brief, and local mathematical tools. Do\nnot search for or read solution-bearing material. Open-web staleness checking is\noutside this run. No claim is made that model pretraining is contamination-free.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
